Being level 12-ish when you find the quest isn't unusual at all. Gaining
levels by killing monsters takes longer with each level, so it's also normal
that you're not levelling up as quick as you like. Generally, at around this
stage it's a good idea to gain a level or two by other means; it won't make
the game too much harder, and as a wizard you want those levels anyway. So,
off the top of my head, some ways to get up to 14, which is the quest
threshold:

	* Quaff Potions of gain level, obviously.
	* Dance with foocubi. Find a sink, kick it until a foocubus comes out,
	  then use it's services until you get to level 14 or he/she gets a
	  "severe headache" (which shouldn't happen too soon). As a wizard,
	  your Int should be high enough to get a good netto level gain out of
	  it. See http://www.nethack.de/spoiler330/succubi.txt (is that the
	  most up to date version?)
	* Eat wraith corpses. When you find a graveyard, lure the wraiths to
	  the stairs. They'll follow you up, where they'll be more likely to
	  leave a corpse.

I especially recommend the second method. I'd personally do that and then go
for the quest right away. The wizard quest is relatively easy and gives you a
really nice artifact.

